## Test Anti-Pattern Audit — Severity-Ranked Findings

This test suite is a textbook example of **"coverage-only" testing** — every production method is called (hitting 95%+ line coverage) but almost nothing meaningful is verified. Here's the ranked list:

---

### 🔴 Critical: Assert-Free Tests (lines 17–21, 33–35, 39–42, 64–66, 69–74, 85–88)

**6 of 10 tests have zero assertions.** They exercise code paths but verify nothing. A method could return garbage or corrupt state and these tests still pass.

**Fix examples:**

```csharp
// AddProduct_Works — verify the product is actually persisted
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(product, retrieved);

// UpdatePrice_Works — verify new price stuck
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")!.Price);

// RemoveProduct_Works — verify product is gone
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));

// GetProductCount_Works — verify count is correct
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
Assert.AreEqual(1, _catalog.GetProductCount());

// ApplyBulkDiscount_Works — verify prices actually changed
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
Assert.AreEqual(8.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")!.Price);
Assert.AreEqual(17.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-002")!.Price);

// ImportFromCsv_Works — verify product was imported
_catalog.ImportFromCsv("SKU-001,Widget,9.99");
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")!.Name);
```

---

### 🟠 High: Weak Assertions — `IsNotNull` on collections (lines 29, 51, 59, 81)

`Assert.IsNotNull(results)` passes even if the list is empty or contains wrong items. These will never fail because `List<T>` and `string` return types are never null here.

**Fix examples:**

```csharp
// GetProduct_Works — verify actual values
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", result!.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, result.Price);

// SearchProducts_Works — verify correct filtering
Assert.AreEqual(1, results.Count);
Assert.AreEqual("SKU-001", results[0].Sku);

// GetAllProducts_Works — verify count and content
Assert.AreEqual(1, all.Count);

// ExportToCsv_Works — verify format
Assert.AreEqual("SKU-001,Widget,9.99", csv);
```

---

### 🟡 Medium: Missing Negative/Edge-Case Tests

No test verifies:
- `UpdatePrice` throws `KeyNotFoundException` for missing SKU
- `GetProduct` returns `null` for non-existent SKU
